{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01364",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.05,
      "end_seconds": 5.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.27,
      "end_seconds": 10.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yes, have a seat. Tell me what's going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.82,
      "end_seconds": 18.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Yeah, it's tightness in my chest when I walk. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.71,
      "end_seconds": 23.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Time for your numbers, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.78,
      "end_seconds": 40.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.83,
      "end_seconds": 72.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.52,
      "text": "Okay: saturation 97 percent, pulse 89, temperature is 36.8 degrees, respiratory rate 17, blood pressure 158 over 92. So, what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.74,
      "end_seconds": 76.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "It's been three weeks now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.26,
      "end_seconds": 81.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Is it a lot or only a little?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.7,
      "end_seconds": 87.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.42,
      "end_seconds": 91.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "What aggravates it, if anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.63,
      "end_seconds": 97.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "Climbing stairs and walking fast definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 98.82,
      "end_seconds": 100.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Does anything help it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.33,
      "end_seconds": 105.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Only stopping to rest, and it's not much."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.66,
      "end_seconds": 111.83,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Is it there all the time or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.81,
      "end_seconds": 116.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'd say every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.85,
      "end_seconds": 121.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.53,
      "end_seconds": 136.22,
      "duration_seconds": 13.69,
      "text": "A heavy feeling in the left arm goes along with it, most of the time. Breathlessness on exertion was there, but it's gone away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.6,
      "end_seconds": 144.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "Have you had tightness in your chest when you walk before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.99,
      "end_seconds": 150.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "A bit, last winter. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.75,
      "end_seconds": 158.29,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any fever or swelling in the ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.8,
      "end_seconds": 163.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "No, no fever or swelling in the ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.08,
      "end_seconds": 170.54,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "I see, go ahead. Have you noticed fainting, cough or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.06,
      "end_seconds": 178.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.21,
      "text": "Hmm, I haven't had fainting, cough or pain at rest, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.68,
      "end_seconds": 184.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.99,
      "end_seconds": 188.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.14,
      "end_seconds": 199.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.65,
      "end_seconds": 214.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "It's metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day. I do miss it now and then, to be fair. I'm on aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.5,
      "end_seconds": 221.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.4,
      "end_seconds": 224.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I've got heart disease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.08,
      "end_seconds": 231.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.85,
      "end_seconds": 235.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.73,
      "end_seconds": 245.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.37,
      "end_seconds": 253.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.73,
      "end_seconds": 255.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.58,
      "end_seconds": 259.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.44,
      "end_seconds": 265.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.72,
      "end_seconds": 268.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.03,
      "end_seconds": 273.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Okay, what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.74,
      "end_seconds": 278.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.66,
      "end_seconds": 282.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "Do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.22,
      "end_seconds": 288.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.85,
      "end_seconds": 294.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Okay, time for me to examine you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.45,
      "end_seconds": 298.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.5,
      "end_seconds": 311.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.52,
      "text": "Lungs are clear and there's no swelling in your ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.99,
      "end_seconds": 314.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.6,
      "end_seconds": 330.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, no murmurs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.54,
      "end_seconds": 332.5,
      "duration_seconds": 0.96,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.99,
      "end_seconds": 349.89,
      "duration_seconds": 14.9,
      "text": "You can sit up now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It's hard to say. Angina-type chest pain is one possibility and a musculoskeletal cause another, and I'd rather not commit yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 351.39,
      "end_seconds": 352.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.12,
      "end_seconds": 362.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like angina-type chest pain, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.68,
      "end_seconds": 380.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "A treadmill test is what I'd like next, for exertional chest tightness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 382.54,
      "end_seconds": 386.07,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I can book that for Wednesday at 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.99,
      "end_seconds": 400.9,
      "duration_seconds": 12.91,
      "text": "I want a lipid profile done, that's for cardiovascular risk. For this, atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night, long term. That should help with cardiovascular risk."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 401.7,
      "end_seconds": 405.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.48,
      "end_seconds": 426.11,
      "duration_seconds": 19.63,
      "text": "Don't push through the chest tightness, stop, sit down, and use the spray if I've given it to you. One warning sign to remember: the chest tightness comes at rest or lasts more than fifteen minutes. In that case don't wait. Let's review you after the results are back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 427.11,
      "end_seconds": 430.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.38,
      "end_seconds": 437.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "So, how would you describe the plan, so we're on the same page?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.24,
      "end_seconds": 448.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "So, I take the atorvastatin, 40 milligrams, at night and come back after the results are back. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.45,
      "end_seconds": 454.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. I think we're done unless you have questions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.13,
      "end_seconds": 458.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 459.75,
      "end_seconds": 460.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}